TASK 4 - WHAT EMBEDDING VECTORS REPRESENT
----------------------------------------------------------------------
An embedding vector is a numerical representation of the semantic meaning of text.
It is not a random ID and it is not simply a count of the keywords in the text.
Texts with similar meanings tend to have vectors that are closer together in vector space.
This allows PharmaLens to retrieve relevant clinical document chunks even when the user's question uses different wording.

